1: # Mocking Guide
2: 
3: ## Overview
4: 
5: Mocking replaces real dependencies with test doubles to isolate code and make tests deterministic. This guide covers mocking strategies for Flutter tests.
6: 
7: ## When to Mock
8: 
9: - Testing code that depends on external services (APIs, databases)
10: - Isolating components for unit tests
11: - Simulating error conditions and edge cases
12: - Making tests faster and more reliable
13: - Testing code that uses plugins
14: 
15: ## Using Mockito
16: 
17: ### Setup
18: 
19: Add to `pubspec.yaml`:
20: 
21: ```yaml
22: dev_dependencies:
23:   build_runner: ^2.10.4
24:   mockito: ^5.6.1
25: ```
26: 
27: ### Generate Mocks
28: 
29: Create a test file with a Mockito annotation and import the generated file:
30: 
31: ```dart
32: import 'package:mockito/annotations.dart';
33: import 'package:mockito/mockito.dart';
34: 
35: import 'user_repository_test.mocks.dart';
36: 
37: @GenerateMocks([ApiClient, UserRepository])
38: void main() {}
39: ```
40: 
41: Generate mocks:
42: 
43: ```bash
44: dart run build_runner build
45: ```
46: 
47: ### Basic Mocking
48: 
49: ```dart
50: import 'package:mockito/annotations.dart';
51: import 'package:mockito/mockito.dart';
52: 
53: import 'my_service_test.mocks.dart';
54: 
55: @GenerateMocks([ApiService])
56: void main() {
57:   late MockApiService mockApiService;
58:   late MyService myService;
59:   
60:   setUp(() {
61:     mockApiService = MockApiService();
62:     myService = MyService(mockApiService);
63:   });
64:   
65:   test('calls API and returns data', () async {
66:     // Arrange
67:     when(mockApiService.fetchData())
68:       .thenAnswer((_) async => {'data': 'value'});
69:     
70:     // Act
71:     final result = await myService.getData();
72:     
73:     // Assert
74:     expect(result['data'], 'value');
75:     verify(mockApiService.fetchData()).called(1);
76:   });
77: }
78: ```
79: 
80: ## Mocking Different Types
81: 
82: ### Mocking Classes
83: 
84: ```dart
85: class DataService {
86:   Future<String> fetchData() async => 'real data';
87: }
88: 
89: // In a real test file, generate MockDataService with @GenerateMocks([DataService]).
90: test('mocks class method', () async {
91:   final mockService = MockDataService();
92:   
93:   when(mockService.fetchData())
94:     .thenAnswer((_) async => 'mocked data');
95:   
96:   final result = await mockService.fetchData();
97:   expect(result, 'mocked data');
98: });
99: ```
100: 
101: ### Mocking Interfaces
102: 
103: ```dart
104: abstract class Storage {
105:   void save(String key, String value);
106:   String? load(String key);
107: }
108: 
109: class FakeStorage implements Storage {
110:   final values = <String, String>{};
111: 
112:   @override
113:   void save(String key, String value) {
114:     values[key] = value;
115:   }
116: 
117:   @override
118:   String? load(String key) => values[key];
119: }
120:

120: 
121: // Test
122: test('uses a fake storage implementation', () {
123:   final storage = FakeStorage();
124:   
125:   storage.save('key', 'value');
126:   
127:   expect(storage.load('key'), 'value');
128: });
129: ```
130: 
131: ### Mocking Streams
132: 
133: ```dart
134: class StreamService {
135:   Stream<int> get counterStream => StreamController<int>().stream;
136: }
137: 
138: // Test
139: test('mocks stream', () async {
140:   final mockService = MockStreamService();
141:   
142:   final controller = StreamController<int>();
143:   when(mockService.counterStream).thenAnswer((_) => controller.stream);
144:   
145:   expectLater(
146:     mockService.counterStream,
147:     emitsInOrder([1, 2, 3]),
148:   );
149:   
150:   controller.add(1);
151:   controller.add(2);
152:   controller.add(3);
153:   await controller.close();
154: });
155: ```
156: 
157: ## Mockito Features
158: 
159: ### Returning Values
160: 
161: ```dart
162: when(mockService.getData()).thenReturn('value');
163: 
164: when(mockService.getUser(id)).thenReturn(User(id: id, name: 'Test'));
165: 
166: when(mockService.getList()).thenReturn([1, 2, 3]);
167: ```
168: 
169: ### Throwing Errors
170: 
171: ```dart
172: when(mockService.getData())
173:   .thenThrow(Exception('Network error'));
174: 
175: when(mockService.saveData(data))
176:   .thenThrow(FormatException('Invalid data'));
177: ```
178: 
179: ### Async Responses
180: 
181: ```dart
182: when(mockService.fetchData())
183:   .thenAnswer((_) async => 'async data');
184: 
185: when(mockService.loadUser(id))
186:   .thenAnswer((_) async => Future.delayed(
187:     const Duration(milliseconds: 100),
188:     () => User(id: id),
189:   ));
190: ```
191: 
192: ### Sequential Returns
193: 
194: ```dart
195: when(mockService.getData())
196:   .thenReturn('first')
197:   .thenReturn('second')
198:   .thenThrow(Exception('error'));
199: 
200: // First call returns 'first'
201: expect(await mockService.getData(), 'first');
202: 
203: // Second call returns 'second'
204: expect(await mockService.getData(), 'second');
205: 
206: // Third call throws
207: await expectLater(mockService.getData(), throwsException);
208: ```
209: 
210: ### Conditional Returns
211: 
212: ```dart
213: when(mockService.getUser(argThat(allOf(isA<String>(), contains('@')))))
214:   .thenReturn(User(email: 'test@example.com'));
215: 
216: when(mockService.getUser(argThat(predicate<String>((arg) => arg.length > 5))))
217:   .thenReturn(User(name: 'Long Name'));
218: 
219: // Matches email format
220: expect(mockService.getUser('test@example.com').email, 'test@example.com');
221: 
222: // Matches length > 5
223: expect(mockService.getUser('Long Name').name, 'Long Name');
224: ```
225: 
226: ### Capturing Arguments
227: 
228: ```dart
229: mockService.save('key1', 'value1');
230: mockService.save('key2', 'value2');
231: 
232: final captured = verify(mockService.save(captureAny, captureAny)).captured;
233: 
234: expect(captured, ['key1', 'value1', 'key2', 'value2']);
235: ```
236: 
237: ## Verification
238: 
239: ### Verify Calls
240: 
241: ```dart
242: mockService.getData();
243: 
244: verify(mockService.getData()).called(1);
245: verify(mockService.getData()).called(greaterThan(0));
246: verifyNever(mockService.otherMethod());
247: ```
248: 
249: ### Verify In Order
250: 
251: ```dart
252: mockService.first();
253: mockService.second();
254: mockService.third();
255: 
256: verifyInOrder([
257:   mockService.first(),
258:   mockService.second(),
259:   mockService.third(),
260: ]);
261: ```
262: 
263: ### Verify Specific Arguments
264: 
265: ```dart
266: mockService.save('key', 'value');
267: 
268: verify(mockService.save('key', 'value')).called(1);
269: verify(mockService.save(argThat(isA<String>()), any)).called(1);
270: ```
271: 
272: ### Verify No More Interactions
273: 
274: ```dart
275: mockService.getData();
276: 
277: verify(mockService.getData()).called(1);
278: verifyNoMoreInteractions(mockService);
279: 
280: verifyNoInteractions(otherMockService);

280: verifyNoInteractions(otherMockService);
281: ```
282: 
283: ## Mocking Platform Channels
284: 
285: ### Basic Platform Channel Mock
286: 
287: ```dart
288: import 'package:flutter/services.dart';
289: 
290: void main() {
291:   TestWidgetsFlutterBinding.ensureInitialized();
292:   
293:   setUp(() {
294:     TestDefaultBinaryMessengerBinding.instance.defaultBinaryMessenger
295:         .setMockMethodCallHandler(
296:       const MethodChannel('com.example.app/channel'),
297:       (MethodCall methodCall) async {
298:         switch (methodCall.method) {
299:           case 'getBatteryLevel':
300:             return 85;
301:           case 'openUrl':
302:             return true;
303:           default:
304:             throw MissingPluginException();
305:         }
306:       },
307:     );
308:   });
309:   
310:   tearDown(() {
311:     TestDefaultBinaryMessengerBinding.instance.defaultBinaryMessenger
312:         .setMockMethodCallHandler(
313:       const MethodChannel('com.example.app/channel'),
314:       null,
315:     );
316:   });
317:   
318:   test('gets battery level', () async {
319:     final platform = MethodChannel('com.example.app/channel');
320:     final result = await platform.invokeMethod('getBatteryLevel');
321:     expect(result, 85);
322:   });
323: }
324: ```
325: 
326: ### Platform Channel with Arguments
327: 
328: ```dart
329: setUp(() {
330:   TestDefaultBinaryMessengerBinding.instance.defaultBinaryMessenger
331:       .setMockMethodCallHandler(
332:     const MethodChannel('com.example.app/storage'),
333:     (MethodCall methodCall) async {
334:       if (methodCall.method == 'save') {
335:         final args = methodCall.arguments as Map;
336:         storage[args['key']] = args['value'];
337:         return true;
338:       } else if (methodCall.method == 'load') {
339:         final args = methodCall.arguments as Map;
340:         return storage[args['key']];
341:       }
342:       return null;
343:     },
344:   );
345: });
346: 
347: test('saves and loads from platform storage', () async {
348:   final platform = MethodChannel('com.example.app/storage');
349:   
350:   await platform.invokeMethod('save', {'key': 'test', 'value': 'data'});
351:   final result = await platform.invokeMethod('load', {'key': 'test'});
352:   
353:   expect(result, 'data');
354: });
355: ```
356: 
357: ## Mocking Repositories
358: 
359: ### Data Repository
360: 
361: ```dart
362: import 'package:mockito/annotations.dart';
363: import 'package:mockito/mockito.dart';
364: 
365: import 'user_repository_test.mocks.dart';
366: 
367: class UserRepository {
368:   final ApiClient apiClient;
369:   
370:   UserRepository(this.apiClient);
371:   
372:   Future<User> getUser(String id) async {
373:     final data = await apiClient.get('/users/$id');
374:     return User.fromJson(data);
375:   }
376: }
377: 
378: @GenerateMocks([ApiClient])
379: void main() {
380:   late MockApiClient mockApiClient;
381:   late UserRepository userRepository;
382:   
383:   setUp(() {
384:     mockApiClient = MockApiClient();
385:     userRepository = UserRepository(mockApiClient);
386:   });
387:   
388:   test('fetches and parses user', () async {
389:     when(mockApiClient.get('/users/123'))
390:       .thenAnswer((_) async => {
391:         'id': '123',
392:         'name': 'John Doe',
393:         'email': 'john@example.com',
394:       });
395:     
396:     final user = await userRepository.getUser('123');
397:     
398:     expect(user.id, '123');
399:     expect(user.name, 'John Doe');
400:     verify(mockApiClient.get('/users/123')).called(1);

400:     verify(mockApiClient.get('/users/123')).called(1);
401:   });
402: }
403: ```
404: 
405: ## Mocking State Management
406: 
407: ### BLoC Mock
408: 
409: ```dart
410: class CounterBloc extends Bloc<CounterEvent, CounterState> {
411:   CounterBloc() : super(CounterInitial()) {
412:     on<IncrementEvent>((event, emit) => emit(CounterIncremented()));
413:   }
414: }
415: 
416: // Test
417: test('emits states on increment', () {
418:   final bloc = CounterBloc();
419:   
420:   expectLater(bloc, emitsInOrder([
421:     CounterInitial(),
422:     CounterIncremented(),
423:   ]));
424:   
425:   bloc.add(IncrementEvent());
426: });
427: ```
428: 
429: ### Provider Mock
430: 
431: ```dart
432: class AuthProvider extends ChangeNotifier {
433:   bool _isLoggedIn = false;
434:   bool get isLoggedIn => _isLoggedIn;
435:   
436:   void login() {
437:     _isLoggedIn = true;
438:     notifyListeners();
439:   }
440: }
441: 
442: // Test
443: test('notifies listeners on login', () {
444:   final provider = AuthProvider();
445:   bool notified = false;
446:   
447:   provider.addListener(() {
448:     notified = true;
449:   });
450:   
451:   provider.login();
452:   
453:   expect(notified, true);
454:   expect(provider.isLoggedIn, true);
455: });
456: ```
457: 
458: ## Manual Mocks
459: 
460: ### Simple Manual Mock
461: 
462: ```dart
463: class ApiService {
464:   Future<String> fetchData() async => 'real data';
465: }
466: 
467: class MockApiService implements ApiService {
468:   String? _mockedResponse;
469:   
470:   void setMockResponse(String response) {
471:     _mockedResponse = response;
472:   }
473:   
474:   @override
475:   Future<String> fetchData() async => _mockedResponse ?? 'default mock';
476: }
477: 
478: // Test
479: test('uses manual mock', () async {
480:   final mockService = MockApiService();

480:   final mockService = MockApiService();
481:   mockService.setMockResponse('test data');
482:   
483:   final result = await mockService.fetchData();
484:   expect(result, 'test data');
485: });
486: ```
487: 
488: ### State-Based Mock
489: 
490: ```dart
491: class StatefulMockService implements ApiService {
492:   final List<String> responses = [];
493:   int _callCount = 0;
494:   
495:   @override
496:   Future<String> fetchData() async {
497:     if (_callCount < responses.length) {
498:       return responses[_callCount++];
499:     }
500:     throw Exception('No more responses');
501:   }
502:   
503:   void addResponse(String response) {
504:     responses.add(response);
505:   }
506: }
507: 
508: // Test
509: test('returns sequential responses', () async {
510:   final mock = StatefulMockService();
511:   mock.addResponse('first');
512:   mock.addResponse('second');
513:   
514:   expect(await mock.fetchData(), 'first');
515:   expect(await mock.fetchData(), 'second');
516:   
517:   await expectLater(mock.fetchData(), throwsException);
518: });
519: ```
520: 
521: ## Best Practices
522: 
523: 1. **Mock at boundaries** - Mock external dependencies, not internal logic
524: 2. **Avoid over-mocking** - Only mock what's necessary for the test
525: 3. **Verify interactions** - Ensure mocks are called correctly
526: 4. **Use specific matchers** - Avoid `any` when possible
527: 5. **Clear expectations** - Make test intentions clear
528: 6. **Reset mocks** - Use setUp/tearDown to clean up
529: 7. **Test real behavior** - Verify expected outcomes, not implementation
530: 8. **Keep mocks simple** - Complex mocks indicate design issues
531: 
532: ## Common Patterns
533: 
534: ### Mock Chain
535: 
536: ```dart
537: when(mockService.first())
538:   .thenReturn(mockSecondService);
539: when(mockSecondService.getData())
540:   .thenReturn('result');
541: 
542: final result = mockService.first().getData();
543: expect(result, 'result');
544: ```
545: 
546: ### Mock Repository
547: 
548: ```dart
549: class MockRepository {
550:   final Map<String, dynamic> _data = {};
551:   
552:   T get<T>(String key) => _data[key] as T;
553:   void set<T>(String key, T value) => _data[key] = value;
554: }
555: 
556: // Test
557: test('uses mock repository', () {
558:   final repo = MockRepository();
559:   repo.set('name', 'John');
560:

560:   
561:   expect(repo.get<String>('name'), 'John');
562: });
563: ```
564: 
565: ### Mock Factory
566: 
567: ```dart
568: class ServiceFactory {
569:   static ApiService create() => RealApiService();
570: }
571: 
572: class MockServiceFactory {
573:   ApiService? mockService;
574:   
575:   ApiService create() => mockService ?? RealApiService();
576: }
577: 
578: // Test
579: test('uses factory mock', () {
580:   final factory = MockServiceFactory();
581:   factory.mockService = MockApiService();
582:   
583:   when(factory.mockService!.getData()).thenReturn('mocked');
584:   
585:   final service = factory.create();
586:   expect(service.getData(), 'mocked');
587: });
588: ```

1: # Unit Testing Guide
2: 
3: ## Overview
4: 
5: Unit tests test individual functions, methods, or classes in isolation. They are the foundation of a well-tested Flutter app, providing fast feedback and high maintainability.
6: 
7: ## When to Write Unit Tests
8: 
9: - Testing business logic functions
10: - Validating data transformations
11: - Testing state management logic (Bloc, Provider, Riverpod)
12: - Mocking external services/API calls
13: - Testing utility functions and helpers
14: 
15: ## Test Structure
16: 
17: ### Basic Test
18: 
19: ```dart
20: import 'package:test/test.dart';
21: 
22: void main() {
23:   test('description', () {
24:     // Arrange
25:     final subject = MyClass();
26:     
27:     // Act
28:     final result = subject.myMethod();
29:     
30:     // Assert
31:     expect(result, expectedValue);
32:   });
33: }
34: ```
35: 
36: ### Group Tests
37: 
38: ```dart
39: import 'package:test/test.dart';
40: 
41: void main() {
42:   group('Counter', () {
43:     late Counter counter;
44:     
45:     setUp(() {
46:       counter = Counter();
47:     });
48:     
49:     test('value starts at 0', () {
50:       expect(counter.value, 0);
51:     });
52:     
53:     test('increment increases value', () {
54:       counter.increment();
55:       expect(counter.value, 1);
56:     });
57:     
58:     tearDown(() {
59:       counter.dispose();
60:     });
61:   });
62: }
63: ```
64: 
65: ## Testing Patterns
66: 
67: ### Testing Pure Functions
68: 
69: ```dart
70: // Function to test
71: int add(int a, int b) => a + b;
72: 
73: // Test
74: test('add returns sum of two numbers', () {
75:   expect(add(2, 3), 5);
76:   expect(add(-1, 1), 0);
77: });
78: ```
79: 
80: ### Testing State Changes

80: ### Testing State Changes
81: 
82: ```dart
83: class Counter {
84:   int _value = 0;
85:   int get value => _value;
86:   
87:   void increment() => _value++;
88:   void decrement() => _value--;
89:   void reset() => _value = 0;
90: }
91: 
92: // Tests
93: group('Counter state changes', () {
94:   late Counter counter;
95:   
96:   setUp(() => counter = Counter());
97:   
98:   test('initial value is 0', () {
99:     expect(counter.value, 0);
100:   });
101:   
102:   test('increment increases value by 1', () {
103:     counter.increment();
104:     expect(counter.value, 1);
105:   });
106:   
107:   test('decrement decreases value by 1', () {
108:     counter.decrement();
109:     expect(counter.value, -1);
110:   });
111:   
112:   test('multiple increments work correctly', () {
113:     counter.increment();
114:     counter.increment();
115:     counter.increment();
116:     expect(counter.value, 3);
117:   });
118: });
119: ```
120: 
121: ### Testing Async Operations
122: 
123: ```dart
124: class DataService {
125:   Future<String> fetchData() async {
126:     await Future.delayed(const Duration(seconds: 1));
127:     return 'data';
128:   }
129: }
130: 
131: // Test
132: test('fetchData returns data after delay', () async {
133:   final service = DataService();
134:   final result = await service.fetchData();
135:   expect(result, 'data');
136: });
137: ```
138: 
139: ### Testing Streams
140: 
141: ```dart
142: class CounterStream {
143:   final _controller = StreamController<int>();
144:   Stream<int> get stream => _controller.stream;
145:   
146:   void increment() => _controller.sink.add(1);
147:   void dispose() => _controller.close();
148: }
149: 
150: // Test
151: test('stream emits values', () async {
152:   final counter = CounterStream();
153:   
154:   expectLater(
155:     counter.stream,
156:     emitsInOrder([1, 1, 1]),
157:   );
158:   
159:   counter.increment();
160:   counter.increment();
161:   counter.increment();
162:   
163:   await Future.delayed(const Duration(milliseconds: 100));
164:   counter.dispose();
165: });
166: ```
167: 
168: ## Matchers
169: 
170: ### Common Matchers
171: 
172: ```dart
173: // Equality
174: expect(actual, equals(expected));
175: 
176: // Not equal
177: expect(actual, isNot(equals(expected)));
178: 
179: // Null checks
180: expect(value, isNull);
181: expect(value, isNotNull);
182: 
183: // Numeric comparisons
184: expect(5, greaterThan(3));
185: expect(5, lessThan(10));
186: expect(5, greaterThanOrEqualTo(5));
187: expect(5, lessThanOrEqualTo(5));
188: 
189: // Type checking
190: expect(obj, isA<String>());
191: expect(obj, isNot(isA<int>()));
192: 
193: // String matching
194: expect(text, contains('substring'));
195: expect(text, startsWith('prefix'));
196: expect(text, endsWith('suffix'));
197: expect(text, matches(RegExp(r'\d+')));
198: 
199: // Lists
200: expect(list, isEmpty);
201: expect(list, isNotEmpty);
202: expect(list, hasLength(3));
203: expect(list, contains(item));
204: expect(list, orderedEquals([1, 2, 3]));
205: ```
206: 
207: ### Custom Matchers
208: 
209: ```dart
210: import 'package:test/test.dart';
211: 
212: class HasLength extends Matcher {
213:   final int expectedLength;
214:   HasLength(this.expectedLength);
215:   
216:   @override
217:   bool matches(item, Map matchState) {
218:     return (item as List).length == expectedLength;
219:   }
220:   
221:   @override
222:   Description describe(Description description) {
223:     return description.add('has length $expectedLength');
224:   }
225: }
226: 
227: // Usage
228: test('list has custom length', () {
229:   final list = [1, 2, 3];
230:   expect(list, HasLength(3));
231: });
232: ```
233: 
234: ## Exception Testing
235: 
236: ```dart
237: class Calculator {
238:   int divide(int a, int b) {
239:     if (b == 0) throw ArgumentError('Cannot divide by zero');
240:     return a ~/ b;
241:   }
242: }
243: 
244: // Test
245: test('divide throws when dividing by zero', () {
246:   final calculator = Calculator();
247:   expect(
248:     () => calculator.divide(10, 0),
249:     throwsArgumentError,
250:   );
251: });
252: 
253: test('divide throws with specific message', () {
254:   final calculator = Calculator();
255:   expect(
256:     () => calculator.divide(10, 0),
257:     throwsA(isA<ArgumentError>()
258:       .having((e) => e.message, 'message', contains('zero'))),
259:   );
260: });
261: ```
262: 
263: ## Mocking
264: 
265: ### Using Mockito
266: 
267: ```dart
268: import 'package:mockito/annotations.dart';
269: import 'package:mockito/mockito.dart';
270: 
271: import 'user_service_test.mocks.dart';
272: 
273: @GenerateMocks([ApiClient])
274: void main() {
275:   group('UserService', () {
276:     late MockApiClient mockApiClient;
277:     late UserService userService;
278:     
279:     setUp(() {
280:       mockApiClient = MockApiClient();
281:       userService = UserService(mockApiClient);
282:     });
283:     
284:     test('fetches user data', () async {
285:       when(mockApiClient.getUser('123'))
286:         .thenAnswer((_) async => User(id: '123', name: 'John'));
287:       
288:       final user = await userService.getUser('123');
289:       
290:       expect(user.name, 'John');
291:       verify(mockApiClient.getUser('123')).called(1);
292:     });
293:   });
294: }
295: ```
296: 
297: Generate the mock file with:
298: 
299: ```bash
300: dart run build_runner build

300:   await tester.tap(find.byType(ElevatedButton)); // Error
301: });
302: 
303: // Solution: Use correct type or use Text finder
304: testWidgets('correct finder', (tester) async {
305:   await tester.pumpWidget(TextButton(child: Text('Button')));
306:   await tester.tap(find.byType(TextButton)); // Correct
307: });
308: ```
309: 
310: ## Plugin/Platform Errors
311: 
312: ### 'MissingPluginException'
313: 
314: **Error Message:**
315: ```
316: MissingPluginException(No implementation found for method MethodName on channel channel.name)
317: ```
318: 
319: **Cause:** Plugin not registered or mock not set up in tests.
320: 
321: **Solution:** Mock the method channel in tests.
322: 
323: ```dart
324: import 'package:flutter/services.dart';
325: 
326: void main() {
327:   TestWidgetsFlutterBinding.ensureInitialized();
328:   
329:   setUp(() {
330:     TestDefaultBinaryMessengerBinding.instance.defaultBinaryMessenger
331:         .setMockMethodCallHandler(
332:       const MethodChannel('your.plugin.channel'),
333:       (MethodCall methodCall) async {
334:         if (methodCall.method == 'getPlatformVersion') {
335:           return 'Android 12';
336:         }
337:         throw MissingPluginException();
338:       },
339:     );
340:   });
341:   
342:   tearDown(() {
343:     TestDefaultBinaryMessengerBinding.instance.defaultBinaryMessenger
344:         .setMockMethodCallHandler(
345:       const MethodChannel('your.plugin.channel'),
346:       null,
347:     );
348:   });
349: }
350: ```
351: 
352: ## Async Errors
353: 
354: ### 'TimeoutException'
355: 
356: **Error Message:**
357: ```
358: TimeoutException after 0:00:05.000000: Test timed out after 5 seconds.
359: ```
360: 
361: **Cause:** Async operation not completing or `pumpAndSettle()` waiting indefinitely.
362: 
363: **Solution:** Set timeout or fix infinite loops.
364: 
365: ```dart
366: // Solution 1: Increase timeout
367: testWidgets(
368:   'long-running test',
369:   (tester) async {
370:     await tester.pumpWidget(MyWidget());
371:     await Future.delayed(const Duration(seconds: 10));
372:   },
373:   timeout: const Timeout(Duration(minutes: 1)),
374: );
375: 
376: // Solution 2: Fix infinite pumpAndSettle
377: testWidgets('fix infinite settle', (tester) async {
378:   await tester.pumpWidget(MyWidget());
379:   await tester.pump(); // Use pump() instead of pumpAndSettle() if animation loops
380: });
381: ```
382: 
383: ## Data Errors
384: 
385: ### 'RangeError'
386: 
387: **Error Message:**
388: ```
389: RangeError: Index out of range: index should be less than 5, but is 5
390: ```
391: 
392: **Cause:** Accessing list/array with invalid index.
393: 
394: **Solution:** Check bounds before access or handle empty cases.
395: 
396: ```dart
397: // Problem
398: testWidgets('range error', (tester) async {
399:   final items = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];
400:   expect(items[5], 6); // Error: index 5 out of range
401: });
402: 
403: // Solution 1: Check bounds
404: testWidgets('safe access', (tester) async {
405:   final items = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];
406:   if (items.length > 5) {
407:     expect(items[5], 6);
408:   }
409: });
410: 
411: // Solution 2: Handle empty lists
412: testWidgets('handle empty list', (tester) async {
413:   final items = <int>[];
414:   if (items.isEmpty) {
415:     expect(find.text('No items'), findsOneWidget);
416:   } else {
417:     expect(items.first, 1);
418:   }
419: });
420: ```
421: 
422: ## Debugging Tips
423: 
424: ### Enable Verbose Logging
425: 
426: ```bash
427: flutter test --verbose
428: ```
429: 
430: ### Take Screenshots in Integration Tests
431: 
432: ```dart
433: import 'package:integration_test/integration_test.dart';
434: 
435: testWidgets('debug with screenshot', (tester) async {
436:   final binding = IntegrationTestWidgetsFlutterBinding.ensureInitialized()
437:       as IntegrationTestWidgetsFlutterBinding;
438: 
439:   await tester.pumpWidget(MyWidget());
440:   await binding.convertFlutterSurfaceToImage();
441:   await tester.pump();
442:   await binding.takeScreenshot('debug-state');
443: });
444: ```
445: 
446: ### Print Widget Tree
447: 
448: ```dart
449: testWidgets('print tree', (tester) async {
450:   await tester.pumpWidget(MyWidget());
451:   debugDumpApp();
452: });
453: ```
454: 
455: ### Use Debug Flags
456: 
457: ```dart
458: testWidgets('debug flags', (tester) async {
459:   debugPrint('Current state: ...');
460:   await tester.pumpWidget(MyWidget());
461:   debugPrint('Widget tree: ${tester.widgetList(find.byType(MyWidget))}');
462: });
463: ```
464: 
465: ## Prevention
466: 
467: ### Use Type Safety
468: 
469: ```dart
470: // Good: Use type-safe access

470: // Good: Use type-safe access
471: final text = tester.widget<Text>(find.byType(Text));
472: 
473: // Avoid: Unsafe casts
474: final text = find.byType(Text).evaluate().first.widget as Text;
475: ```
476: 
477: ### Check Before Actions
478: 
479: ```dart
480: testWidgets('safe tap', (tester) async {
481:   await tester.pumpWidget(MyWidget());
482:   
483:   final button = find.byType(ElevatedButton);
484:   if (button.evaluate().isNotEmpty) {
485:     await tester.tap(button);
486:   } else {
487:     fail('Button not found');
488:   }
489: });
490: ```
491: 
492: ### Handle All Cases
493: 
494: ```dart
495: testWidgets('comprehensive', (tester) async {
496:   await tester.pumpWidget(MyWidget());
497:   
498:   // Check all possible states
499:   if (find.text('Loading').evaluate().isNotEmpty) {
500:     // Handle loading state
501:   } else if (find.text('Error').evaluate().isNotEmpty) {
502:     // Handle error state
503:   } else {
504:     // Handle success state
505:   }
506: });
507: ```

1: # Integration Testing Guide
2: 
3: ## Overview
4: 
5: Integration tests test complete apps or large parts of apps on real devices or emulators. They verify that all widgets and services work together as expected and can measure performance.
6: 
7: ## When to Write Integration Tests
8: 
9: - Testing complete user flows across multiple screens
10: - Verifying navigation between pages
11: - Testing state persistence
12: - Validating real device behavior (sensors, camera, etc.)
13: - Performance profiling and benchmarking
14: - Testing platform-specific features
15: 
16: ## Setup
17: 
18: ### Add Dependency
19: 
20: Add to `pubspec.yaml`:
21: 
22: ```yaml
23: dev_dependencies:
24:   integration_test:
25:     sdk: flutter
26:   flutter_test:
27:     sdk: flutter
28: ```
29: 
30: ### Create Test Driver
31: 
32: Create `test_driver/integration_test.dart` when using `flutter drive`, browser
33: integration tests, screenshots, or response data from performance traces:
34: 
35: ```dart
36: import 'package:integration_test/integration_test_driver.dart';
37: 
38: Future<void> main() => integrationDriver();
39: ```
40: 
41: ## Test Structure
42: 
43: ### Basic Integration Test
44: 
45: ```dart
46: import 'package:flutter/material.dart';
47: import 'package:flutter_test/flutter_test.dart';
48: import 'package:integration_test/integration_test.dart';
49: import 'package:my_app/main.dart';
50: 
51: void main() {
52:   IntegrationTestWidgetsFlutterBinding.ensureInitialized();
53:   
54:   testWidgets('app launches and displays home', (tester) async {
55:     await tester.pumpWidget(const MyApp());
56:     
57:     expect(find.text('Home Screen'), findsOneWidget);
58:   });
59: }
60: ```
61: 
62: ### Running Integration Tests
63: 
64: ```bash
65: # Run on all devices
66: flutter test integration_test/
67: 
68: # Run on specific device
69: flutter test -d <device-id> integration_test/my_test.dart
70: 
71: # Run specific test file
72: flutter test integration_test/my_test.dart
73: 
74: # Run a browser/driver integration test
75: flutter drive \
76:   --driver=test_driver/integration_test.dart \
77:   --target=integration_test/my_test.dart \
78:   -d chrome
79: ```
80: 
81: ## Testing User Flows
82: 
83: ### Multi-Screen Navigation
84: 
85: ```dart
86: testWidgets('complete user flow from login to dashboard', (tester) async {
87:   await tester.pumpWidget(const MyApp());
88:   
89:   // Login screen
90:   expect(find.text('Login'), findsOneWidget);
91:   
92:   // Enter credentials
93:   await tester.enterText(find.byKey(const Key('username')), 'user@example.com');
94:   await tester.enterText(find.byKey(const Key('password')), 'password123');
95:   
96:   // Tap login
97:   await tester.tap(find.byKey(const Key('login-button')));
98:   await tester.pumpAndSettle();
99:   
100:   // Dashboard screen
101:   expect(find.text('Dashboard'), findsOneWidget);
102:   expect(find.text('Welcome, user@example.com'), findsOneWidget);
103: });
104: ```
105: 
106: ### Tab Navigation
107: 
108: ```dart
109: testWidgets('navigate between tabs', (tester) async {
110:   await tester.pumpWidget(const MyApp());
111:   
112:   // Initial tab
113:   expect(find.text('Home'), findsOneWidget);
114:   
115:   // Tap second tab
116:   await tester.tap(find.text('Profile'));
117:   await tester.pumpAndSettle();
118:   
119:   expect(find.text('Home'), findsNothing);
120:   expect(find.text('Profile'), findsOneWidget);
121:   
122:   // Navigate back
123:   await tester.tap(find.text('Home'));
124:   await tester.pumpAndSettle();
125:   
126:   expect(find.text('Home'), findsOneWidget);
127: });
128: ```
129: 
130: ## Testing Forms
131: 
132: ### Complete Form Submission
133: 
134: ```dart
135: testWidgets('submit registration form', (tester) async {
136:   await tester.pumpWidget(const MyApp());
137:   
138:   // Navigate to registration
139:   await tester.tap(find.text('Sign Up'));
140:   await tester.pumpAndSettle();
141:   
142:   // Fill form
143:   await tester.enterText(find.byKey(const Key('name')), 'John Doe');
144:   await tester.enterText(find.byKey(const Key('email')), 'john@example.com');
145:   await tester.enterText(find.byKey(const Key('password')), 'password123');
146:   await tester.enterText(find.byKey(const Key('confirm-password')), 'password123');
147:   
148:   // Submit
149:   await tester.tap(find.byKey(const Key('submit')));
150:   await tester.pumpAndSettle();
151:   
152:   // Verify success
153:   expect(find.text('Registration Successful'), findsOneWidget);
154: });
155: ```
156: 
157: ### Form Validation
158: 
159: ```dart
160: testWidgets('form shows validation errors', (tester) async {
161:   await tester.pumpWidget(const MyApp());
162:   
163:   await tester.tap(find.text('Sign Up'));
164:   await tester.pumpAndSettle();
165:   
166:   // Submit empty form
167:   await tester.tap(find.byKey(const Key('submit')));
168:   await tester.pump();
169:   
170:   // Verify errors
171:   expect(find.text('Name is required'), findsOneWidget);
172:   expect(find.text('Email is required'), findsOneWidget);
173:   expect(find.text('Password is required'), findsOneWidget);
174:   
175:   // Fill with invalid email
176:   await tester.enterText(find.byKey(const Key('email')), 'invalid-email');
177:   await tester.tap(find.byKey(const Key('submit')));
178:   await tester.pump();
179:   
180:   expect(find.text('Invalid email format'), findsOneWidget);
181: });
182: ```
183: 
184: ## Testing Lists and Data
185: 
186: ### Loading and Displaying Data
187: 
188: ```dart
189: testWidgets('load and display items from API', (tester) async {
190:   await tester.pumpWidget(const MyApp());
191:   
192:   // Wait for data load
193:   await tester.pumpAndSettle();
194:   
195:   // Verify items loaded
196:   expect(find.byType(ListTile), findsWidgets);
197:   expect(find.text('Item 1'), findsOneWidget);
198:   expect(find.text('Item 2'), findsOneWidget);
199: });
200: ```
201: 
202: ### Pull-to-Refresh
203: 
204: ```dart
205: testWidgets('pull to refresh updates list', (tester) async {
206:   await tester.pumpWidget(const MyApp());
207:   await tester.pumpAndSettle();
208:   
209:   // Pull down
210:   await tester.drag(
211:     find.byType(RefreshIndicator),
212:     const Offset(0, 300),
213:   );
